---
/**
 * /programmes/career-preparation/focused-mock-interview/ — from the 15 October 2026 landing-page package
 * (docs/2026-10-15_living-craft-landing-pages/programmes/career-preparation/focused-mock-interview/index.html).
 * Staging only: branch feat/programme-pathways must not merge.
 *
 * The markup and the words are the package's, unchanged, except:
 *   * every fee, hour count and the instructor line read from
 *     src/data/programme-offers.ts and facts.ts (PRICING REVIEW: the fees are
 *     not yet calibrated; see that file's header);
 *   * the instructor line reads "Walmart Labs", as the package has it
 *     (approved by the user on 15 October; facts.ts still says "Walmart");
 *   * the enquiry form is RouteForm (the pipeline), not the package's
 *     email draft. See PackageEnquiry.astro for what that dropped.
 * The look is the package's own stylesheet, scoped: see
 * src/styles/templates/programme-package.css.
 */
import PackagePage from '../../../components/programmes/PackagePage.astro';
import PackageEnquiry from '../../../components/programmes/PackageEnquiry.astro';
import { practitioner } from '../../../data/facts';
import { EXPERIENCE, OFFERS, hourWord, hoursWord, offerLine } from '../../../data/programme-offers';

const o = OFFERS['focused-mock-interview'];

const title = 'Mock Interview with Sunil Mathew | The Living Craft';
const description = `Practise one agreed interview round with ${practitioner.name} and receive specific feedback. A ${o.hours}-hour focused mock for experienced professionals, priced at ${o.fee}.`;
---

<PackagePage title={title} description={description} path="/programmes/career-preparation/focused-mock-interview/" breadcrumb={['Programmes', 'Career Preparation']} enquire="request-a-focused-mock" cta="Request a focused mock">
<section class="hero mock-hero">
<div class="hero-copy">
<div class="offer-line">
<p>
<strong>{offerLine('focused-mock-interview')}</strong>
</p>
</div>
<h1>Practise one interview round.<br>
<span>Get specific feedback.</span>
</h1>
<p>Prepare for an agreed interview theme with Sunil Mathew. Work through the discussion, review your reasoning and leave with clear priorities for further practice.</p>
<p>
<a href="#request-a-focused-mock">Request a focused mock</a>
</p>
</div>
<div class="mock-human">
<figure class="portrait mock-portrait">
<img src="/programmes/sunil-bookshelf.webp" width="480" height="600" alt="Sunil Mathew seated in front of a bookshelf" loading="lazy">
</figure>
</div>
</section>
<section class="section mock-problem" id="make-your-experience-easier-to-assess">
<div class="section-head">
<h2>Make your experience easier to assess</h2>
</div>
<div class="section-body">
<p>You may know your work deeply and still find it difficult to explain under interview conditions. A focused mock gives you a setting to practise how you frame the problem, discuss trade-offs and demonstrate your contribution.</p>
<p>The session examines your approach through one agreed interview theme. Feedback helps you identify what to strengthen before your next round.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section class="section mock-fit" id="who-this-session-is-for">
<div class="section-head">
<h2>Who this session is for</h2>
</div>
<div class="section-body">
<ul>
<li>Experienced engineers preparing for a system-design or project discussion.</li>
<li>Engineering managers and leaders preparing to explain decisions, team work and technical judgment.</li>
<li>Experienced candidates targeting MAANG or other product-company roles who know the round they want to practise.</li>
</ul>
<p>The session is especially relevant to experienced service-company engineers preparing for a move. Experienced professionals from product companies and global capability centres can also discuss fit.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section class="section mock-session" id="what-happens-in-the-session">
<h2>What happens in the session</h2>
<div class="mock-stages">
<article>
<span class="mock-stop" aria-hidden="true">01</span>
<h3>Agree the interview theme</h3>
<p>Share your target role and the round you want to practise. Supported themes can include system design, a project retrospective or engineering leadership, subject to fit.</p>
</article>
<article>
<span class="mock-stop" aria-hidden="true">02</span>
<h3>Work through the mock</h3>
<p>Practise responding to the problem and explaining the choices behind your answer. Use relevant examples from your experience and discuss the trade-offs.</p>
</article>
<article>
<span class="mock-stop" aria-hidden="true">03</span>
<h3>Review your approach</h3>
<p>Receive feedback on your reasoning, communication and relevant gaps. Identify the points to work on in your next practice session.</p>
<p>The mock and feedback are included within the {hourWord(o.hours)} session.</p>
</article>
</div>
</section>
<section class="section mock-outcome" id="what-you-leave-with">
<div class="section-head">
<h2>What you leave with</h2>
</div>
<div class="section-body">
<p>Specific feedback on one interview round and a clearer view of what to improve. The session helps you focus further practice on the gaps that appeared in the discussion.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section class="section mock-evidence" id="practise-with-sunil-mathew">
<div class="section-head">
<h2>Practise with Sunil Mathew</h2>
</div>
<div class="section-body">
<p>Sunil brings {EXPERIENCE}. His background includes hiring, developing and assessing senior engineers, architects and engineering leaders.</p>
<p>The session uses that experience to examine how you explain your work and approach an engineering discussion.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section class="section faq" id="questions-before-booking">
<h2>Questions before booking</h2>
<div>
<details>
<summary>Can I request a mock directly?<span aria-hidden="true">+</span>
</summary>
<div class="answer">
<p>Yes. Share the theme and role you are preparing for. A fit discussion confirms whether the session matches your needs. A Career Readiness Review is optional.</p>
</div>
</details>
<details>
<summary>Does this include interview feedback?<span aria-hidden="true">+</span>
</summary>
<div class="answer">
<p>Yes. Both practice and feedback fit within the {hourWord(o.hours)} session. The focus is on one agreed theme.</p>
</div>
</details>
<details>
<summary>What if I need a preparation plan and more practice?<span aria-hidden="true">+</span>
</summary>
<div class="answer">
<p>
<a href="/programmes/career-preparation/interview-preparation-and-practice/">Interview Preparation and Practice</a> includes one planning session and two mocks within {hoursWord(OFFERS['interview-preparation-and-practice'].hours)} of one-to-one sessions.</p>
</div>
</details>
<details>
<summary>Who is eligible for this service?<span aria-hidden="true">+</span>
</summary>
<div class="answer">
<p>The current service is for experienced engineers and engineering leaders. Freshers are outside its scope.</p>
</div>
</details>
<details>
<summary>Which interview themes can I practise?<span aria-hidden="true">+</span>
</summary>
<div class="answer">
<p>Discuss system design, a project retrospective or engineering leadership during the fit conversation. Coding-round coverage is outside the listed themes.</p>
</div>
</details>
<details>
<summary>Are referrals or placement included?<span aria-hidden="true">+</span>
</summary>
<div class="answer">
<p>The session covers interview practice and feedback. Job applications, referrals and placement are outside its scope.</p>
</div>
</details>
</div>
</section>
<PackageEnquiry
  id="request-a-focused-mock"
  heading="Request a focused mock"
  intro="Share your target role and the round you want to practise. The team will discuss technical fit, availability and payment terms before booking."
  action="Send my mock-interview enquiry"
  labels={{"name":"Full name","email":"Email address","role":"Current role","phone":"Phone number, optional","question":"Target role and interview theme","timing":"Interview timing, optional"}}
  order={["name","email","role","question","timing","phone"]}
  omit={["organisation","discovery","discovery_detail"]}
  fixed={{ interest: o.slug }}
  include={["timing"]}
/>
<div class="related">
<p>
<a href="/programmes/career-preparation/">Compare career packages</a> · <a href="/programmes/">View both pathways</a>
</p>
</div>
</PackagePage>
